// Pixel art as data: one character per pixel, '.' is clear, every other
// character is a palette key. Authored with a scratch generator, then
// committed as plain grids: edit the rows here directly.
//
// Chapter 2-2, Red-Eye: the dream above the clouds, moonlit. Tiles as the
// rooftop set (16 x 16, anchor top left, variants with fps 0): roofTop a
// lumpy moonlit cloud top, roofEdgeLeft and roofEdgeRight its soft round
// ends, roofFill the deep blue-grey body, oneWay a thin wisp, brick a dense
// puff with a crack (breakable), stone a dark storm-cloud block, spikes a
// storm cloud with lightning standing up (hazard), vent an updraft, pipe a
// contrail segment (tileable sideways).
//
// puff (the thin cloud that puffs away): 16 x 16, anchor top left. solid
// when nobody stands on it, wobble while stood on (loop), gone plays once
// as it bursts (then draw nothing until it returns).
//
// Decor anchor is the bottom left. cloudTower is scenery only (a step
// darker than the floor). wingLight frames are variants: 0 red on, 1 red
// off, 2 green on, 3 green off. runwayLights (the goal): the approach
// strobe runs toward the threshold bar over frames 0 to 2, frame 3 the bar
// flares; loop it.
//
// CLOUD_BACKDROP: 512 px tileable strips: far (stars, the moon and its
// halo over a flat cloud sea), mid (the rolling cloud sea), near (the
// plane's wing passing, engine glow, nav light and strobe). navLights gives
// the near strip's light pixels so the renderer can blink them.
import type { Grid, Palette, SpriteSet } from './types';
import type { RooftopTile } from './rooftop';

